    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33915" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">păropsis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">părap-</span></b> ), ĭdis,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παροψίς</span> (prop. a
		side dish), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a large
				square dish for the dessert</i>, <i>a
				dessert-dish;</i> also <i>a small dish</i> in
			gen., <i><span class="en">Juv.
				3, 142</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 27, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Galb. 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Isid. 16, 20, 4</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 50</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">parapsidem proicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 34</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 34, 2, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt.
				23, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 23</span></i>.</div>
